  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Automated Carbon Intensity Reporting for a midstream operator subject to EPA OOOOb/c methane rules, Subpart W reporting, and voluntary frameworks (OGMP 2.0, GHG Protocol). Stakeholders include the Chief Sustainability Officer (corporate decarb plan, investor disclosures, CDP/TCFD/CSRD reporting), VP EH&S (LDAR program execution, leak repair backlog), and Operations (compressor-station emission factors, fugitive methane). Industry context: best-in-class midstream methane intensity is <0.20%; carbon intensity ~5-8 kg CO2e/boe; OGMP 2.0 Gold Standard requires Level 4-5 measurement-based reporting.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Total CO2e = co2e_metric_tons on emission_readings; total_co2e_tons in metric view\n- Methane = methane_tons on emission_readings; primary GHG driver\n- Carbon intensity = carbon_intensity_kg_boe; industry-leading <8 kg/boe\n- Methane intensity = methane_intensity_pct on carbon_kpi_monthly; OGMP Gold target <0.20%\n- Leaks = leak_count on carbon_snapshots; LDAR campaign indicator\n- Reduction target = reduction_target_tons; vs. corporate net-zero plan\n- Offset credits = offset_credits_tons; voluntary or compliance offsets\n- Compliance status = compliance_status (Compliant / Warning / Non-Compliant vs. thresholds)\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - emission_readings_metrics (source: emission_readings) — dims: reading_date, source_id, emission_category, facility_type, measurement_method; measures: total_co2e_tons, total_methane_tons, avg_carbon_intensity, total_throughput_boe, max_co2e_metric_tons.\n  - carbon_snapshots_metrics (source: carbon_snapshots) — dims: snapshot_date, source_id, emission_category, facility_type; measures: total_monthly_co2e, total_leaks, total_offset_credits, avg_reduction_target, max_monthly_co2e_tons.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. source_name, methane_intensity_pct, compliance_status, reduction_target_tons, measurement_method).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show monthly total CO2e by facility type for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 emission sources by total methane tons year-to-date.",
    "Which facilities have a carbon intensity above the company average, and what is the throughput at each?",
    "How has total leak count trended month-over-month across the network?",
    "What is the total offset credits by emission category this year?",
    "Top 10 emission sources by average carbon intensity in kg per boe.",
    "Which emission categories are flagged Non-Compliant on compliance status, and what monthly CO2e do they represent?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in total methane tons?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', reading_date) AS month, MEASURE(total_methane_tons) AS total_methane_tons",
